;;   Every record of a type with defaults gets them when it is made, by
;;   the type's initialization procedure (expected-vax-VaxFields.mar),
;;   called with the record's address: PUSHL, CALLS #1, through G^ for
;;   another module's type. Not a copy (Copy: MOVC3 only).
;; - Module variables, in the initializer, and locals, after the frame is
;;   cleared, in declaration order with the variable initializers: n's
;;   and copy's defaults, h's, then seen := n.serial (line 17), then
;;   lab's and anonymous's; in Local, first := F.counter (line 29), then
;;   q's, in's and arr's. The address is MOVAB of the variable into a
;;   register from R2, which a call keeps.
;; - NEW (Make): once the pointer holds the block, and not when there is
;;   none (MOVL R0, R2; BNEQ over a JMP L^ past it). A record's block is
;;   the record; a fixed array's elements start the block; an open array's
;;   follow its lengths (DataOffset, 8 for two), their count the lengths
;;   multiplied, read from the slots NEW kept them in.
;; - An array of records is a loop: the address and the count in two
;;   registers from R2, pinned, the procedure called for each element,
;;   the address advanced by the element's size, DECL, and BLEQ over a JMP
;;   L^ back, which reaches any distance. A fixed array of arrays is
;;   counted whole (MOVL #2 for arr, #4 for points).
;; - Labelled extends VaxFields.Named: its procedure calls Named's first
;;   (G^), then sets label and size (start + 2, a constant of the module).
;;   Inner, declared in Local, and the anonymous record have procedures of
;;   this module only, -anon<n>, private: a local label and .WORD mask, as
;;   a private procedure's (section 7). Inner's default uses Local's
;;   constant base.
